# Addition laws of bidegree `(3, 3)` on `E^♮`: fibre corrections and the `Φ` identities

Model (`NaturalModel`): `E^♮ ⊂ X = V(F, G) ⊂ ℙ⁴`, coordinates `(U, V, W, T₁, T₃)`,
`G = W T₃ − V T₁ + 2U²`; on `E^♮`, `T₁ = W t`, `T₃ = V t − 2U²/W` (`t = w − ζ(z)`).

For `i ∈ {1, 2}` (the `E`-laws `lawᵢ` of bidegree `(2, 2)`) and multipliers `λ, μ ∈ {V, W}`
the law (`NaturalLaws.NLaw`) is
```
( 2M·lawᵢU, 2M·lawᵢV, 2M·lawᵢW,
  2μ(Q)·lawᵢW·T_λ(P) + 2λ(P)·lawᵢW·T_μ(Q) − κᵂ,
  2μ(Q)·lawᵢV·T_λ(P) + 2λ(P)·lawᵢV·T_μ(Q) − κⱽ ),      M = λ(P) μ(Q),
```
with `T_V = T₃`, `T_W = T₁`. This file defines the fibre corrections `κᵂ = kapWᵢλμ`,
`κⱽ = kapVᵢλμ` (bidegree `(3, 3)` forms in the `E`-variables only, integer coefficients) and proves
`phiᵢλμ`: `Φ = lawᵢV κᵂ − lawᵢW κⱽ + 4M lawᵢU² = q₁ F(P) + q₂ F(Q)` with explicit cofactors.

On `E × E`, `κᵂ = M lawᵢW m − 2μ lawᵢW ρ_λ − 2λ lawᵢW ρ_μ` and
`κⱽ = M (lawᵢV m + 4 lawᵢU²/lawᵢW) − 2μ lawᵢV ρ_λ − 2λ lawᵢV ρ_μ`, where
`m = (y₁ − y₂)/(x₁ − x₂)`, `ρ_V = 2U²/W`, `ρ_W = 0` (`NaturalLawsAff`).
Generated by `gen_lean.py` (sympy), see `VECEXT_SPIKE.md`.
-/

